--- !u!114 &1004139799
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1004139797}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "This is where I begin to unravel the mystery. There must be something
    documenting the case.  Between 1625 and 1627, Malta underwent its witch craze.
    This is when also the trial of forty witches before Inquisitor Onorato Visconti
    took place. But what I am searching for is different. It does not concern old
    wise women, prostitutes, or poor Muslim slaves, the common victims of witchcraft
    accusations, like Betta Caloiro and her promiscuous demon, Farfarello. The victim
    I am researching is a nun, an extremely rare occasion. The principal officer
    is very helpful and points me to the right direction. Leafing through dusted
    volumes, I manage to find the register of the trial. The accused was a 27-year-old
    woman named Sophia Darra. She was charged with having consorted with the devil
    and performed spells in the presence of witnesses. Yet there are no witnesses
    named or mentioned. I cannot even find the verdict. It is as if the trial was
    recorded merely to comply with required formalities but all the important details
    were omitted. I find myself at a dead-end. I am not ready to give up, not yet.
    There is one other place that may hold information: the seat of the Malta Inquisition
    Tribunal in the second capital of the island.\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3dab4aaee5eb57b49bb411e395a45278, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -5798611287592534813, guid: 3dab4aaee5eb57b49bb411e395a45278, type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
  m_fontMaterials: []
